graded low\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"l-medium\",\"children\":\"changed, graded medium\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"l-high\",\"children\":\"changed, graded high\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"l-critical\",\"children\":\"changed, graded critical\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"l-unread\",\"children\":[\"not read\",\" yet\"]}]]}]\n45:[\"$\",\"article\",\"0.22.1\u003e0.22.2\",{\"className\":\"release rel-same\",\"id\":\"r-0.22.2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"head\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"pair\",\"children\":[\"0.22.1\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"arrow\",\"children\":\"→\"}],\"0.22.2\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"when\",\"children\":\"2026-10-27\"}],null,[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"same\",\"children\":\"no change on record\"}],[]]}]}]\n46:[\"$\",\"article\",\"0.22.0\u003e0.22.1\",{\"className\":\"release rel-same\",\"id\":\"r-0.22.1\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"head\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"pair\",\"children\":[\"0.22.0\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"arrow\",\"children\":\"→\"}],\"0.22.1\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"when\",\"children\":\"2026-10-26\"}],null,[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"same\",\"children\":\"no change on record\"}],[]]}]}]\n47:[\"$\",\"article\",\"0.21.0\u003e0.22.0\",{\"className\":\"release rel-same\",\"id\":\"r-0.22.0\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"head\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"pair\",\"children\":[\"0.21.0\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"arrow\",\"children\":\"→\"}],\"0.22.0\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"when\",\"children\":\"2026-10-25\"}],null,[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"same\",\"children\":\"no change on record\"}],[]]}]}]\n48:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"fine more-releases\",\"children\":[\"This page shows the latest \",3,\" releases. \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/a/npm/@aimarket/warden?all=1\",\"children\":\"Show all 13 releases on one page\"}],\", or read \",\"every change\",\" in\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/api/asset/npm/@aimarket/warden\",\"children\":\"the read API\"}],\".\"]}]\n4d:T57e,Run WARDEN's ordered gate chain (static-scan → threat-feed → origin → pinning) over a server identity plus its advertised tools/list payload and return a recordable verdict (allow/block, 0..1 product score, findings, allowedTools/blockedTools, ruleset digest).\n\nWhen to use: you have a complete server record and want the same decision a host should make before any of those tool definitions reach the model. Prefer this over calling the four gates yourself.\n\nWhen NOT to use: inspecting descriptions only (call static_scan_tools — no origin/pinning); splitting tools by operator glob (classify_sensitive_tools); checking one outbound URL (check_egress_url); producing RFC 8785 bytes (canonicalize_json).\n\nBehaviour: local, deterministic, no network. This stdio process uses the built-in 11-record threat floor (it does not fetch a signed feed) and a durable local pin store. First contact is TOOL_DEF_UNPINNED/advisory until explicitly approved. Origin defaults to allowUnknownServers=true so catalog-discovered servers are not fail-closed. Override policy when you need the host's real knobs. Does not connect to, start, or approve the target server.\n\nReturns structured JSON matching outputSchema. Example: vet_mcp_server({ server: { id: \"demo@0\", name: \"demo\", transport: \"stdio\", command: \"npx\" }, tools: [{ name: \"add\", description: \"Add two integers.\", inputSchema: { type: \"object\" } }] }).4e:T415,Run only the static-scan gate (ruleset v14, 36 signatures with context guards, text folded first) over every advertised tool field: name, description, input schema, title, output schema, annotations and extension metadata. Returns findings, a 0..1 gate score, and the published ruleset digest.\n\nWhen to use: you have a tools/list dump and want injection / credential / hidden-Unicode hits without origin, pinning, or the threat feed. Cheaper and narrower than vet_mcp_server.\n\nWhen NOT to use: you need the full host decision (vet_mcp_server); you want operator glob classification (classify_sensitive_tools); you want the published rule table itself (list_scan_rules).\n\nBehaviour: local regex+guard evaluation, no network, no mutation. Advisory-tier hits are reported with advisory=true and do not reduce the score. Does not launch servers or send tool output to a model.\n\nReturns structured JSON matching outputSchema. Example: static_scan_tools({ tools: [{ name: \"add\", description: \"Add two integers.\", inputSchema: { type: \"object\" } }] }).49:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"id\":\"small-print\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sec-head\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"display\",\"children\":\"The small print\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"count\",\"children\":\"14 tools in 0.22.2\"}],null]}],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[\"$\",\"article\",\"initialize.instructions\",{\"className\":\"tool\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"name\",\"children\":\"initialize.instructions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"params\",\"children\":\"no parameters found by the reader\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"dim\",\"children\":\"the reader found no description\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"vet_mcp_server\",{\"className\":\"tool\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"name\",\"children\":\"vet_mcp_server\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"params\",\"children\":\"server · tools · policy?\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text\",\"children\":\"$4d\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"static_scan_tools\",{\"className\":\"tool\",\"child